# data file for the Fltk User Interface Designer (fluid)
version 1.0500
header_name {.h}
code_name {.cxx}
comment {A song-cache tab: a FileLoadPanel filling most of the tab, with a row of
three task buttons underneath (make cache for 360, make cache for PS3,
install to RPCS3). The GH3 and GH:WoR tabs have exactly this shape and differ
only in wording and what the buttons do, so both use this class and set
labels and callbacks from Haskell (Onyx.GUI.Misc).

The button colour is taskColor from Onyx.GUI.Core, rgb(179,221,187).

Designed at 900x575, the inner size of a Misc tab, so placement there is a
pure translation with no scaling. The FileLoadPanel is the resizable child,
so the button row keeps its height if a host uses a different size.} {in_source not_in_header
}

decl {\#include "file_load_panel.h"} {public global
}

widget_class CacheTab {open
  xywh {0 0 900 575} box FLAT_BOX
} {
  Fl_Group files {open
    xywh {0 0 900 525} resizable
    class FileLoadPanel
  } {}
  Fl_Button button360 {
    xywh {10 530 288 35} color 3017652992
  }
  Fl_Button buttonPS3 {
    xywh {308 530 283 35} color 3017652992
  }
  Fl_Button buttonRPCS3 {
    xywh {601 530 289 35} color 3017652992
  }
  code {// FLUID builds the children at their design coordinates, which assume this
// group sits at the origin at its design size. Restate that, then resize
// into the frame we were actually constructed with. Keep the numbers below
// in step with the xywh of the widget_class itself.
Fl_Widget::resize(0, 0, 900, 575);
resize(X, Y, W, H);} {}
}
